            <ArticleTitle>Synovial chondromatosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare case of synovial chondromatosis of the knee occurring in a 65-year-old man is reported. Electron microscopy of the lesion suggests that the cartilaginous nodules develop through a process of metaplasia from the stromal fibroblasts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
